Title: Into the Pyramid
Order: 14
Production Code: 1x14

EXT. EXPEDITION CAMP - DAY

AMB: subdued camp noise

The mail brings the news [[Reuel Briggs]] has been dreading: [[Dianthe Lusk]], drowned, weeks ago, on the Charles River. He collapses. For three weeks [[Professor Stone]] and [[Charlie Vance]] nurse him through a breakdown too total for words.

REUEL BRIGGS
(hollow, to no one)
Many waters cannot quench love, neither can the floods drown it.

EXT. MEROE - NIGHT (LATER)

SFX: oars in still water

Alone, without telling anyone, Reuel rows himself back across to the ruins by moonlight, revolver in hand, no plan beyond losing himself in the pyramid the way he's lost everything else.

INT. GREAT PYRAMID - NIGHT

SFX: footsteps echoing in a vast empty chamber

He descends past glass cases of the ancient dead, searching for the Sphinx head the parchment described — and finds it, unmoving to every instrument the expedition owns, but not, somehow, to him.

A hand seems to pass before his face out of the darkness, trailing a strange sweetness.

REUEL BRIGGS
(faint)
What—

He falls.

INT. TELASSAR - RECEIVING CHAMBER - DAY (FOUR DAYS LATER)

AMB: fountains, distant music, an unfamiliar hush

Reuel wakes on silk cushions in a marble hall that has no business existing. [[Ai]] stands over him.

AI
You've slept the whole crossing. That's usual, the first time.

REUEL BRIGGS
Where is this?

AI
Telassar. You won't have heard the name. Almost no one outside these walls has, in six thousand years.
